0..75 Comment "// Stratified families: a node may hold a function from its own family, the"
76..154 Comment "// family standing to the left of an arrow, because the constructor gives that"
155..230 Comment "// occurrence a stage strictly below the node\'s — Guermond and Nadathur\'s"
231..308 Comment "// stratification read through the accessibility of Guo, Hagens, Kop and Vale"
309..381 Comment "// . A case on a link reads its fields one stage below the link\'s, or at"
382..459 Comment "// a fresh stage for a link at none, so the test a link holds takes the chain"
460..518 Comment "// before it and never the link itself. What refuses is in"
519..560 Comment "// `../../pathological/data/curry.gandr`."
561..563 Comment "//"
564..578 Comment "// - see: #517"
